{
  "slug": "superpowers-optimized",
  "name": "Superpowers Optimized",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Built on the trusted obra/superpowers workflow and refined through research into LLM agent behavior, it adds automatic 3-tier workflow routing, proactive safety hooks, self-consistency verification at critical decision points, cross-session memory, and adversarial red-teaming — everything the original does, plus the discipline layer it was missing.\n\nCross-session memory changes the experience fundamentally. Without it, every session starts blind: the AI re-explores structure it already mapped, re-proposes approaches that were already rejected, re-debugs errors that were already solved. With the four-file memory stack, it arrives knowing what was tried, what was decided, and why — and builds forward instead of sideways.\n\nFive research-backed principles run throughout: *less is more* (minimal always-on instructions), *fresh context beats accumulated context* (subagents get clean scoped prompts, not polluted history), *compliance ≠ competence* (instructions must be carefully engineered, not just comprehensive), *verify your own reasoning* (multi-path self-consistency catches confident-but-wrong failures before they become expensive), and *accountability drives accuracy* (agents that know their output has real downstream consequences perform better).",
  "longDescription": "Ships **24 skills**, **2 agents** and **6 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (24): `brainstorming` (MUST USE when the user wants new features, behavior changes, refactoring with new capabilities, or architecture decisions and…), `claude-md-creator` (Creates minimal, high-signal CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md context files based on empirical best practices), `context-management` (Use in long or noisy sessions to persist durable state across session boundaries via state.md), `deliberation` (Use BEFORE brainstorming when facing a complex architectural, technology, or design decision where the options are not yet…), `dependency-management` (MUST USE when updating, migrating, or auditing project dependencies: upgrading packages, fixing security vulnerabilities (CVEs), resolving breaking changes,…), `dispatching-parallel-agents` (Use when 2+ tasks are independent and can run concurrently without file or state conflicts or sequential dependencies), `error-recovery` (Maintains a project-specific known-issues.md mapping recurring errors to their solutions), `executing-plans` (MUST USE when a plan.md exists and implementation needs to begin), and 16 more\n- **Agents** (2): `code-reviewer` (Use this agent to review completed implementation work against requirements, correctness, and production readiness), `red-team` (Use this agent to adversarially attack completed implementation work — find concrete ways to break the code through…)\n- **Hooks** (6): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SubagentStop`, `PreToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install superpowers-optimized@claude-community` from `REPOZY/superpowers-optimized`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 24,
    "agent": 2,
    "hook": 6
  },
